{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports", "label": "ADR 0009: One contract, two transports", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_one_contract_two_transports", "label": "One contract, two transports", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Live mode asks four questions by route name and gets {ok, status, body} back over a same-origin GET (serve_live.py) or an invoke() left on window.__DVD_BRIDGE__ by the Forge adapter; the page cannot tell which it has. Body shapes are the contract; status is transport-level. Letting resolvers return their own shape and reshaping in the page was refused as one product behaving differently depending on how it was reached."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_bridge_adapter", "label": "Forge bridge adapter (window.__DVD_BRIDGE__)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CommonJS, requires @forge/bridge inside a try because the SDK throws outside a Forge iframe; must be a classic script linked ahead of app.js because app.js decides at load which transport it has and an ES module is deferred."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_resolver_plays_fetcher_not_calculator", "label": "The resolver plays the fetcher's part, not the calculator's", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "statusCategory and started are absent over the bridge because deciding what a status means is organisation config; the resolver sends raw statusTransitions and the page decides. addedMidSprint IS read from the changelog because it needs no config and defaulting it to false would be a plausible wrong number (full marks for scope stability)."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_no_page_text_reaches_jira", "label": "No text from the page reaches Jira", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only caller-supplied input is a context id; parseContextId refuses anything not canonical, so the app can issue only three date pairs per board built by the resolver from its own clock. Justifies read:jql:jira."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports", "target": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_one_contract_two_transports", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports", "target": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_bridge_adapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports", "target": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_resolver_plays_fetcher_not_calculator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0009-one-contract-two-transports.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports", "target": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports_no_page_text_reaches_jira", "relation": "re